Volumes: 

root volume: where the OS saved

**Snapshot**
--> snapshot is a point in time image of EBS volume.
--> two ways:
1. manual backup
2. automatic backup 

    --> to migrate an EBS from one AZ to another then create snapshot and create volume 
    from the snapshot in the intended AZ.
    --> EBS snapshot is an incremental backup.
    --> the first backup of a volume backups all the data.
    --> every next backup copies only a block of data that has changed since the last snapshot.

